# What this deployment allows, which is the browser's own surface and nothing else.
#
# The board reads files it shipped with and asks the browser for no device: no camera, no microphone, no location, no
# notifications, no clipboard, no serial or USB. A feature that needs one is refused by the policy rather than prompted
# for, so a reader is never asked to hand a device to a demonstration. Fullscreen and autoplay stay available because
# the frame's own controls use them.
/*
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), clipboard-read=(), clipboard-write=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), notifications=(), payment=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
